      <p class="text-emerald-900">
        The Federal Skilled Worker Program (FSWP) is one of the three programs you can qualify for through Express Entry. You need at least one year of continuous skilled work in NOC TEER 0 to 3 in the last 10 years, CLB 7 in English or French, education (with an ECA if it is foreign), usually proof of funds, and at least 67 out of 100 on the FSW selection grid. Meeting those rules only gets you into the pool: invitations go by CRS score, and in 2026 IRCC held no general all-program rounds, so most FSW candidates abroad need a category, a high-wage job offer or a provincial nomination to stand out.
